{"baseRefName":"master","body":"## Summary\n\nFixes the issue where agents pulled into another agent's thread (via @mention) would stop receiving messages after their initial mention.\n\n## Problem\n\nWhen Effie is @mentioned in Galen's thread, she responds correctly. But subsequent messages directed at Effie (without an explicit @mention) are ignored — only Galen processes them because he owns the thread. The message gate (`mentioned || in_own_thread || is_dm || is_reply_to_bot`) would reject the message for all non-owner agents.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdded `thread_participant?` detection:\n1. After the channel context is determined, if the agent isn't the thread owner and wasn't directly mentioned, check the thread history (last 50 messages)\n2. If the bot was previously mentioned OR posted in the thread, it's a 'participant'\n3. Thread participants pass through to the intent check, which then determines if the message is directed at them\n\nThis means:\n- Thread owner (Galen): processes via `in_own_thread`, uses intent check to decide ✓\n- Thread participant (Effie): processes via `is_thread_participant`, uses intent check to decide ✓  \n- Uninvolved agents: still rejected at the gate (never mentioned/posted in thread) ✓\n\n## Testing\n\nAdded 4 tests:\n- Bot previously mentioned in thread history → participant\n- Bot previously posted in thread history → participant\n- Bot absent from history → not participant\n- API error handling → safe fallback (not participant)\n\nAll 48 tests pass.\n\n## Related\n\nPaired with stowzilla/brainiac#12 for intent prompt improvements.","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOTMjnus8AAAABJKEi3Q","author":{"login":"ardavis"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Fix rubocop","createdAt":"2026-07-07T22:11:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"EYES","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/stowzilla/brainiac-discord/pull/3#issuecomment-4909507293","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"headRefName":"discord-intent-fix-1720389132","title":"Enable thread participants to receive messages via intent check"}
